# Message Retry Flow

                  LOCAL MESSAGE
                       │
                       ▼
                    PENDING
                       │
                       ▼
                   SENDING
                       │
            ┌──────────┼──────────┐
            │          │          │
          ACK      transient   permanent
            │        error       error
            ▼          │          ▼
          SENT         │        FAILED
                       │
                 retry/backoff
                       │
                  attempt 2
                       │
                 retry/backoff
                       │
                  attempt 3
                       │
              ┌────────┴────────┐
              │                 │
           success          exhausted
              │                 │
             SENT             WAIT
                                │
                    ┌───────────┼───────────┐
                    │           │           │
                 reconnect      |       foreground
                    │           │           │
                    └───────────┴───────────┘
                                │
                          new retry cycle

- Retry `messages sequentially` within each conversation, while allowing `bounded concurrency` across conversations with maximum of 3 active conversations.
- Do not start retry cycle if network is not available.

---

## Transient Error

- No network
- Socket disconnected
- Request timeout
- Temporary server error

## Permanent Error

- Invalid payload
- Invalid content type
- Unauthorized
- Not a conversation participant
- Conversation permanently unavailable

- `Transient` failure ≠ `FAILED`.
- Permanent server rejection -> `FAILED` immediately.

---

## Retry/Exponential Backoff

- Each send attempt has a `timeout` of `5s`.
- Maximum 3 `automatic` attempts per `retry` cycle.
- `Transient` failures get `exponential backoff`.
- `Exhausting` a cycle does not `fail` the `message`.
- Other `messages` can `continue` after the cycle is `exhausted`.

---

## Retry Triggers

- Socket `reconnects`.

3 attempts exhausted
↓
message remains retryable
↓
WAIT
│
├── Socket reconnect
├── Network available
├── App foreground
↓
start new retry cycle

- Prevent `multiple` triggers from starting `concurrent` retry cycles for the same `message`.
- `in-flight coordination`, So only one delivery attempt is active for a give `clientId`.

